### 8. **src/Mod/Part/App/FeatureExtrusion.cpp:263** — `getShape` default options include `Transform`, but caller may not want it

**Failure scenario**: `calculateShapeNormal` calls `getShape(shapeLink.getValue(), nullptr, &mat, &docobj)` relying on default `options = ResolveLink | Transform`. The `Transform` flag causes `obj->getSubObject(nullptr, nullptr, &topMat)` to overwrite `topMat` with the object's placement, then `shape.transformShape(topMat)` applies it. But the caller also receives `*pmat = topMat * mat` and may apply it again, double-transforming the normal.

```cpp
// New getShape default: options = ResolveLink | Transform
TopoDS_Shape sh = Feature::getShape(shapeLink.getValue(), nullptr, &mat, &docobj);
// shape already transformed by object placement via Transform flag
// *pmat also includes object placement → caller may double-apply
```

Old code had `transform=true` default too, so this is pre-existing, but the new explicit flag structure makes it easier to accidentally enable.

